  "evidence": "- TEXT_E: Neighbourhood policing in every community; create the Serious Organised Crime Agency; tougher penalties on guns and knives; secure borders with biometrics and ID cards; robust counter‑terror laws. Triple NHS spending, 18‑week treatment target, cleanliness and prevention (smoke‑free workplaces, healthier school meals). \"Rights matched by responsibilities,\" make work pay via minimum wage and tax credits, incapacity benefit reform, extend patient choice. Single Equality Act and new Commission on Equality and Human Rights; reduce child and pensioner poverty; devolution and stronger local government. Pro‑EU leadership with a constitutional treaty referendum; retain independent nuclear deterrent; NATO central to defence.\n- TEXT_F: 5,000 extra police per year; zero‑tolerance neighbourhood policing; 20,000 extra prison places; end early release; honesty in sentencing; elected police commissioners. Border Control Police, 24‑hour port surveillance, Australian‑style points system, withdraw from the 1951 Convention, and an annual, Parliament‑approved immigration limit. School authority and discipline: heads control admissions/expulsions; Turnaround Schools; tougher exams and a slimmer curriculum. NHS: bring back Matron to close wards for cleaning; infection control; more single rooms; funding follows the patient; end waiting lists; support carers; contribution for self‑funders. Proportionality/value: cut waste/quangos; lower taxes; money follows the pupil; free places at independent schools; link basic pension to earnings; promote saving via Lifetime Savings Accounts. National sovereignty/loyalty: referendum to reject the EU Constitution; no Euro; preserve regiments and warships; English votes for English laws.",
